    },
    {
      "text": "6. Conclusions",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        466.0439147949219,
        166.72848510742188,
        476.7916259765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The method of scenario optimization offers a partial solution to the lack of correctness guarantees",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        487.6466369628906,
        522.0001220703125,
        497.39935302734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for data-driven approaches to reachability analysis. We have found that several simple Monte Carlo-",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        501.1956481933594,
        522.0001831054688,
        510.9483642578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "type approaches to approximating reachable sets can be put on a solid foundation and supplied with",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        514.74462890625,
        522.0001831054688,
        524.4973754882812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "probabilistic guarantees of correctness by framing them as scenario optimization problems. In this",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        528.294677734375,
        522.0001831054688,
        538.0474243164062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "paper we have focused on two variants of the case of approximation by norm balls, which lead to",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        541.8436279296875,
        522.0001831054688,
        551.5963745117188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "scalable sample complexities and efﬁciently-solvable optimization problems.",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        555.3926391601562,
        425.9237365722656,
        565.1453857421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "However, the scenario optimization approach has two limitations. First, the reachable set ap-",
      "bbox": [
        106.93600463867188,
        568.941650390625,
        522.0052490234375,
        578.6943969726562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "proximations must be convex sets, since the scenario optimization guarantee will not hold otherwise.",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        582.4906005859375,
        522.0,
        592.2433471679688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Second, the requirement that the scenario optimization problem be constructed from iid samples",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        596.0396118164062,
        522.000244140625,
        605.7923583984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "precludes this approach from providing guarantees for active learning-based approaches, in which",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        609.589599609375,
        522.0001831054688,
        619.3423461914062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "case the sample distribution would have correlations.",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        623.1386108398438,
        321.0764465332031,
        632.891357421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
